Bot desktop: Debian 13, Google Chrome, and an Xfce panel on
 every display

Bot computers run Debian 13 with Google Chrome and an Xfce desktop: the
xfwm4 window manager and one bottom panel (Applications, Browser, File
Manager, Terminal, open windows, clock) on each bot's existing display.
Packages install at image build time as root, before the runtime user and
NSS wrapper apply. Each display gets its own D-Bus session and its own panel
settings under ~/.config/rakazo-desktop, written once and kept afterwards.
The session also answers to `fluxbox`, so the runtime's per-display start
and stop commands drive it unchanged; starting it again on a display
replaces the earlier session there, and it cleans up only its own processes.

